> with atom ids <-> with attachment points: C1C2CCNCC2CCC1 <-> [CH:4]1[CH:5]2[CH2:6][CH:7][N:21][CH2:22][CH:23]2[CH2:24][CH:25][CH:28]1 <-> [2*]C1C([29*])C([26*])CC2CN([20*])C([8*])CC21, \\n", "function_name": "describe_high_level_fg_fragments", "arguments": {"smiles": "COC(=O)C1C2CC3c4[nH]c5cc(OC)ccc5c4CCN3CC2CC(OC)C1OC"}}\\nassistant\\n\\n<think>\\nInteresting. The molecule contains an indole moiety, a decahydroisoquinoline (fused ring system), carboxylic ester, ethers, and an NH group. This looks like a complex natural product-like molecule. Let\'s compute some properties relevant to BBB penetration.\\n\\nKey factors for BBB penetration: molecular weight, lipophilicity (logP), polar surface area (TPSA), hydrogen bond donors/acceptors, rotatable bonds, etc. Let\'s gather data.\\n\\nFirst, molecular weight. Use get_molecular_weight.\\n</think>\\n<|action_start|><|plugin|>\\n{"name": "get_molecular_weight", "parameters": {"smiles": "COC(=O)C1C2CC3c4[nH]c5cc(OC)ccc5c4CCN3CC2CC(OC)C1OC"}}\\n<|action_end|>\\nenvironment name=<|plugin|>\\n\\n{"result": "Average molecular weight (Daltons): 428.5290", "function_name": "get_molecular_weight", "arguments": {"smiles": "COC(=O)C1C2CC3c4[nH]c5cc(OC)ccc5c4CCN3CC2CC(OC)C1OC"}}\\nassistant\\n\\n<think>\\nMolecular weight is 428.5 Da, which is above the typical cutoff for good BBB penetration (usually <500 Da, but many CNS drugs are <400). This is borderline.\\n\\nExact molecular weight? Use get_exact_molecular_weight.\\n</think>\\n<|action_start|><|plugin|>\\n{"name": "get_exact_molecular_weight", "parameters": {"smiles": "COC(=O)C1C2CC3c4[nH]c5cc(OC)ccc5c4CCN3CC2CC(OC)C1OC"}}\\n<|action_end|>\\nenvironment name=<|plugin|>\\n\\n{"result": "Exact molecular weight (Daltons): 428.2311", "function_name": "get_exact_molecular_weight", "arguments": {"smiles": "COC(=O)C1C2CC3c4[nH]c5cc(OC)ccc5c4CCN3CC2CC(OC)C1OC"}}\\nassistant\\n\\n<think>\\nNow logP (Wildman–Crippen cLogP). Use get_mol_logp.\\n</think>\\n<|action_start|><|plugin|>\\n{"